Kavis build marker.

live-build copies includes.chroot into the chroot BEFORE it runs the
normal hooks, so this file exists inside the build chroot and on the
built system, and NOWHERE ELSE. Every hook that edits the running
system refuses to start without it (see the "Host guard" block at the
top of iso/config/hooks/normal/*.hook.chroot).

Reason: on 4 September 2026 a Kavis hook ran on the development
Codespace instead of the chroot; /home and the user account were
damaged badly enough that the container had to be rebuilt. A hook that
rewrites /home, /etc/passwd, sudoers, initramfs or systemd state must
never be able to run on a developer machine by accident.

Do not delete this file and do not create it by hand on a workstation.
